  "notes" : [
    {
      "note" : "# Basic Color Plane\n\n### Intro\nThis sample illustrates simple rendering concepts in Fabric\n\nAnything rendered to the screen uses a Mesh node eventually!\n\nA Mesh combines Geometry (the 2D or 3D shape data) and the Material (how the surface of the geometry is shaded, textured and lit).\n\n\nA Mesh Node adjusts the position, scale and orientation of the Geometry connected to it. \n\nFabric comes out of the box with various Geomety and Material nodes to combine. \n\n### Adjusting Values with the Inspector\nTo adjust a nodes values\n1. First select a node by clicking on it in the canvas \n2. Make sure the right sidebar \/ property inspector is visible (you can use the top right toolbar button to toggle the inspector)\n3. Inspect and adjust node values in the inspector. \n\nTry adjusting the color of the material, and the size of the geometry.\n\n\n### Next Steps\n\n* Try opening the left sidebar and clicking the “Mesh” Square icon.\n* This will reveal available Geometry and Materials you can use.\n* Create other Geometry nodes and connect them.\n* Create other Material nodes and connect them.\n",
      "id" : "5EFDB3D4-0CB5-4C59-A4F3-9170B3A7D2F2",
      "rect" : [
        [
          -567.97265625,
          -311.6484375
